<title>GERMANY: German trade estimates recent wheat sales to CIS.</title>
<headline>German trade estimates recent wheat sales to CIS.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia and Uzbekistan are estimated to have bought at least 100,000 tonnes of new crop West European wheat, mostly German, so far this season, traders estimated on Thursday.</p>
<p>Future business intentions were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Earlier traders said Poland has bought up to 500,000 tonnes of West European wheat since September, again nearly all from Germany.</p>
</text>
